<div id="Sx5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx5.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Overall, Y-RAG’s hybrid retrieval and support filtering strategy exhibits excellent domain adaptation on pathology corpora.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx5.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx5.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Question–answering performance evaluation</span>  Tables <a href="#Sx5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Experiments ‣ YpathRAG: A Retrieval–Augmented Generation Framework and Benchmark for Pathology" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Sx5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Experiments ‣ YpathRAG: A Retrieval–Augmented Generation Framework and Benchmark for Pathology" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> present results on YpathQA-M for general and medical LLMs. Across all metrics, Y-RAG significantly improves answer generation quality.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx5.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="Sx5.p9.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">General models</em> (Table <a href="#Sx5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Experiments ‣ YpathRAG: A Retrieval–Augmented Generation Framework and Benchmark for Pathology" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>): GPT-4o, Qwen2, and DeepSeek-R1-7B consistently benefit from Y-RAG, achieving average gains of 6.2%–9.0%. Notably, GPT-4o-Y-RAG achieves 0.9477 in Faithfulness, reflecting improved factual reliability.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx5.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx5.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="Sx5.p10.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Medical models</em> (Table <a href="#Sx5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Experiments ‣ YpathRAG: A Retrieval–Augmented Generation Framework and Benchmark for Pathology" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>): Improvements are even more pronounced for medical-specific LLMs. HuatuoGPT-Y-RAG attains 0.9528 Faithfulness, while PMC-LLaMA and LLaVA-Med exhibit 10%–15% gains in Coverage and Semantic similarity. These results confirm that Y-RAG’s retrieval enhancement effectively bridges domain knowledge gaps and enhances the professionalism and completeness of generated answers.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx5.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx5.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx5.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation studies</span>  We further analyze the impact of candidate pool size and context segment number through systematic ablation experiments, as shown in Figs. <a href="#Sx5.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Experiments ‣ YpathRAG: A Retrieval–Augmented Generation Framework and Benchmark for Pathology" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and <a href="#Sx5.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ Experiments ‣ YpathRAG: A Retrieval–Augmented Generation Framework and Benchmark for Pathology" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx5.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx5.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="Sx5.p12.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Candidate segment number (<math id="Sx5.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>)</em>: Expanding the candidate pool from Top–10 to Top–30 increases both Coverage and Faithfulness, indicating richer evidence recall. However, when <math id="Sx5.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K&gt;30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K&gt;30</annotation></semantics></math>, Keyword precision declines slightly due to noise from irrelevant candidates. The best balance occurs at <math id="Sx5.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=20</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx5.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx5.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="Sx5.p13.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Context segment number (<math id="Sx5.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>)</em>: Performance rises notably when <math id="Sx5.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> increases from 1 to 3—Faithfulness and Semantic similarity improve by 2.3% and 1.6%, respectively. When <math id="Sx5.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;3</annotation></semantics></math>, performance plateaus or slightly decreases, suggesting that excessive context can distract the generator from the main evidence.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx5.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx5.p14.1" class="ltx_p">Overall, Y-RAG achieves optimal factual completeness and semantic conciseness when the context remains within a moderate range.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx5.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx5.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx5.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Module fine–tuning and implementation details</span>  In the filtering module, we fine–tuned Qwen2.5-Instruct-7B as a binary discriminator on YpathR’s positive and negative pairs. LoRA-based parameter-efficient tuning (rank 16) was applied with a learning rate of <math id="Sx5.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> and batch size of 1. The fine-tuned filter achieved stable validation performance, substantially improving support discrimination and ensuring reliable evidence for answer generation.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx5.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx5.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx5.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Summary</span>  Y-RAG significantly outperforms existing methods in both retrieval and QA, establishing new state-of-the-art results on YpathR and delivering consistent improvements across both general and medical LLMs. The pathology vocabulary and LoRA-based LLM filter are key contributors to these gains.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Sx5.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.08603v1/top_trend_balanced_labelclose.svg" id="Sx5.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/334;" width="476" height="334"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx5.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="Sx5.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Ablation study: effect of the number of candidate passages (<math id="Sx5.F7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>) on model performance.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx5.F8" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.08603v1/ctx_trend_balanced_labelclose.svg" id="Sx5.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/334;" width="476" height="334"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx5.F8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="Sx5.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Ablation study: effect of the number of context passages (<math id="Sx5.F8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>) on model performance.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="Sx6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Conclusion</h2>

<div id="Sx6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we introduced two benchmarks—YpathR and YpathQA-M—for systematically evaluating retrieval and question-answering capabilities in pathology scenarios. Building on these, we proposed Y-RAG, a pathology-specific retrieval-augmented generation framework that integrates multi-channel hybrid retrieval with a LoRA-based support filtering module.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Experimental results demonstrate that Y-RAG achieves substantial gains in retrieval precision and answer quality, outperforming strong baselines across both general and medical LLMs. This work provides a reproducible and domain-adapted paradigm for applying RAG frameworks in pathology, paving the way for reliable and interpretable medical AI systems.</p>
</div>
</section>
